{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"x":0.20975389666484867,"y":0.10875695684592879,"w":0.053743235270182321,"h":0.013590737422588206,"c":1,"t":"Test 4"},{"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.2098765443420984,"w":0.26954732259114589,"y":0.14958775027473514,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2"},{"c":1,"y":0.18016413153503907,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.2096659697448563,"h":0.022103450042760597,"w":0.72260233561197906},{"w":0.14814814249674479,"t":"Passage 2 below.","h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"y":0.19611307444714376,"x":0.20781893269538615},{"c":1,"x":0.45637259122938206,"y":0.23088429548118827,"h":0.021743826085462437,"t":"Why zoos are good","w":0.23328043619791666},{"y":0.26265496264751298,"c":1,"x":0.34758199479239049,"h":0.018161513078058356,"w":0.45094716389973954,"t":"Scientist David Hone makes the case for zoos"},{"c":1,"t":"In my view, it is perfectly possible for many species of animals living in zoos","x":0.23442594962640953,"w":0.63608744303385423,"y":0.28755833837046763,"h":0.019267049638907574},{"y":0.30341453362392512,"t":"or wildlife parks to have a quality of life as high as, or higher than, in the wild.","x":0.24678380641929021,"h":0.019018386643121055,"w":0.63812596638997399,"c":1},{"h":0.019940280801977517,"y":0.31822983650103387,"c":1,"x":0.2446854456436669,"t":"Animals in good zoos get a varied and high-quality diet with all the supplements","w":0.65876520792643234},{"x":0.24472856675255361,"y":0.33411244875049095,"w":0.67926767985026038,"h":0.019228882447007933,"c":1,"t":"required, and any illnesses they might have will be treated. Their movement might"},{"x":0.2447421963105873,"h":0.017934639686970955,"y":0.35023974921755818,"c":1,"w":0.65040598551432272,"t":"be somewhat restricted, but they have a safe environment in which to live, and"},{"h":0.01964906528504351,"x":0.24467631902155879,"c":1,"t":"they are spared bullying and social ostracism by others of their kind. They do not","w":0.66906178792317705,"y":0.36453777955153843},{"h":0.019365089380558587,"t":"suffer from the threat or stress of predators, or the irritation and pain of parasites or","y":0.38064121623332769,"w":0.68750823974609365,"c":1,"x":0.24472255315872918},{"y":0.39496440358183216,"h":0.018495696733921818,"c":1,"x":0.2447095683529841,"t":"injuries. The average captive animal will have a greater life expectancy compared","w":0.67312830607096352},{"w":0.66886952718098969,"h":0.017448068086334367,"c":1,"x":0.24477357801039318,"t":"with its wild counterpart, and will not die of drought, of starvation or in the jaws of","y":0.41218776153831427},{"w":0.68131078084309904,"h":0.019376434622720762,"c":1,"x":0.24473982957116561,"y":0.42661786467169915,"t":"a predator. A lot of very nasty things happen to truly wild' animals that simply don't"},{"y":0.44054727830919371,"x":0.24682663187903206,"t":"happen in good zoos, and to view a life that is 'free' as one that is automatically","w":0.6524361673990885,"h":0.01879324087405787,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.45630336773738844,"h":0.023052770482075768,"t":"'good' is, I think, an error. Furthermore, zoos serve several key purposes.","x":0.24248419012881395,"w":0.60755304972330726},{"h":0.018781420479674571,"t":"Firstly, zoos aid conservation. Colossal numbers of species are becoming extinct","y":0.4803137620100526,"c":1,"w":0.6690374755859374,"x":0.2426436617606032},{"x":0.24476440273245695,"y":0.49793381547684601,"h":0.017541466949966167,"c":1,"w":0.65860697428385417,"t":"across the world, and many more are increasingly threatened and therefore risk"},{"h":0.018309593200683594,"t":"extinction. Moreover, some of these collapses have been sudden, dramatic and","y":0.51279885576827466,"w":0.65249471028645833,"x":0.24678210409069889,"c":1},{"t":"unexpected, or were simply discovered very late in the day. A species protected","x":0.24472997062864976,"c":1,"w":0.65456217447916665,"y":0.52819012537322907,"h":0.018904657891838483},{"x":0.24270557181646515,"w":0.66272593180338546,"c":1,"y":0.54425150946628953,"t":"in captivity can be bred up to provide a reservoir population against a population","h":0.017710603729715335},{"x":0.24472146103341874,"c":1,"w":0.68132766723632809,"t":"crash or extinction in the wild. A good number of species only exist in captivity, with","h":0.018359558321140668,"y":0.55893743193605305},{"y":0.57473818140053046,"w":0.65036814371744789,"h":0.017023520138294668,"c":1,"t":"many of these living in zoos. Still more only exist in the wild because they have","x":0.24272420014983576},{"c":1,"w":0.64836786905924471,"h":0.017834036032920442,"t":"been reintroduced from zoos, or have wild populations that have been boosted","x":0.24268095190993194,"y":0.59006283203999299},{"t":"by captive bred animals. Without these efforts there would be fewer species alive","y":0.60542965807253557,"x":0.24266019201635336,"h":0.017240210893718633,"w":0.66897079467773446,"c":1},{"y":0.62048309953945857,"x":0.24058285695950096,"c":1,"w":0.65873092651367182,"h":0.01968887472882852,"t":"today. Although reintroduction successes are few and far between, the numbers"},{"y":0.63647228432577174,"h":0.017095547823237522,"t":"are increasing, and the very fact that species have been saved or reintroduced as a","w":0.68742385864257805,"c":1,"x":0.24476208651690362},{"t":"result of captive breeding proves the value of such initiatives.","w":0.50858469645182303,"x":0.2405710474508182,"h":0.018595076562097468,"c":1,"y":0.65080351018783944},{"t":"Zoos also provide education. Many children and adults, especially those in cities,","h":0.0182493140194806,"c":1,"y":0.67555953028683691,"w":0.66490290323893231,"x":0.24470811339334811},{"x":0.24470890092509934,"y":0.6902783887953845,"t":"will never see a wild animal beyond a fox or pigeon. While it is true that television","w":0.66489608764648434,"h":0.018207348418039171,"c":1},{"w":0.62156402587890625,"y":0.70723449244821257,"c":1,"x":0.24476392222674595,"h":0.015493783849709453,"t":"documentaries are becoming ever more detailed and impressive, and many"},{"x":0.24269654889378092,"h":0.017548782384578132,"c":1,"t":"natural history specimens are on display in museums, there really is nothing to","y":0.72198811684065023,"w":0.64630167643229175},{"h":0.020385885968786877,"c":1,"t":"compare with seeing a living creature in the flesh, hearing it, smelling it, watching","w":0.66903330485026036,"y":0.73705664026546946,"x":0.24057545036779004},{"t":"what it does and having the time to absorb details. That alone will bring a greater","x":0.24270946140885277,"y":0.75273904520625634,"w":0.66478418986002608,"h":0.01665189044354809,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"understanding and perspective to many, and hopefully give them a greater","x":0.24268472471073513,"y":0.76835945595729938,"w":0.61336542765299484,"h":0.016785962561976953},{"c":1,"x":0.24271008482910267,"y":0.78370784920581393,"t":"appreciation for wildlife, conservation efforts and how they can contribute.","h":0.017193459509679987,"w":0.60513336181640631},{"x":0.19958847746006245,"y":0.86482558123800246,"w":0.024691357612609877,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"86","c":1}]}